# Day 3 lint/format toolchain. Kept in its own environment, separate from
# backend/.venv, so that installing ruff/black/mypy/vulture/radon cannot drift
# the environment requirements.txt is reconciled against. Never committed:
# it is developer tooling, not a project dependency.
# Also covers .venv-repro-day3/, the throwaway environment the Day 3
# reproducibility check builds and deletes.
.venv-*/
.day3/node_modules/

# Post-coding harnesses. `.day2/` and `.day3/` ARE committed — they are the
# evidence the POSTCODING_DAY_0*.md records cite, and a reader should be able
# to re-run them. Three things inside them are excluded:
#
#   .day2/backup/  holds a copy of the LIVE corpus (the SQLite row store, the
#                  ChromaDB vectors and 3 real uploaded PDFs) taken so Day 2
#                  could restore the baseline after destructive probes. It is
#                  user data, excluded for exactly the reason backend/data/ is.
#   *.day2fix      stale copies of application source, kept only to diff
#   *.before-day3  against during that day. The real files are tracked.
#   .day2/*.out    captured server stdout — same category as *.log.
.day2/backup/
*.day2fix
*.before-day3
.day2/*.out

# Audit report generated against the project (post-coding Day 6). It is a
# working document about the repository rather than part of the application,
# and the decision was taken deliberately to keep it out of the published
# repository rather than to leave it untracked by accident — the schedule PDF
# §10 requires every file in `git ls-files` to be one that was intended.
PROJECT_COMPLETE_AUDIT_REPORT.pdf

