# ── Deliberately NOT ignored ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# backend/tests/fixtures/*.pdf  (8 files, 157 KB total)
#
# These are committed on purpose, even though `make_fixtures.py` can regenerate
# them. test_retriever.py asserts measured similarity scores against this exact
# corpus (RELEVANT_SCORE_FLOOR = 0.50, UNRELATED_SCORE_CEILING = 0.30).
# Regenerating with a different PyMuPDF version can shift glyph layout, hence
# extracted text, hence embeddings, hence those scores — which would turn a
# green suite red on a fresh clone for reasons that have nothing to do with the
# code. 157 KB is a trivial repository cost for a test suite that runs
# immediately after `git clone` with no extra steps. The generator stays
# committed for provenance; the PDFs stay committed as the fixed reference
# corpus.
